[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 500,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 539,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69725,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 227,
        "headingId": 539,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Littr&eacute; gland adenocarcinoma is a tumour originating in the periurethral glands of the penile urethra.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:08:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 501,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 540,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69726,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 227,
        "headingId": 540,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8140/3 Carcinoma of Littr&eacute; glands</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:08:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 502,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 541,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69727,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 227,
        "headingId": 541,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2C93.0 &amp; XH22Z8 Adenocarcinoma of urethra or paraurethral gland &amp; Carcinoma of Skene, Cowper, and Littr&eacute; glands</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:08:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 503,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 542,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69728,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 227,
        "headingId": 542,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> urethral accessory gland adenocarcinoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:08:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 504,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 543,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69729,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 227,
        "headingId": 543,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:08:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 505,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 544,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69730,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 227,
        "headingId": 544,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours are localized in the penile urethra {13160939; 1113396; 26410973}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:08:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 506,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 545,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69731,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 227,
        "headingId": 545,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The main clinical symptoms are bloody or mucous urethral discharge, haematospermia, haematuria, and a palpable mass. Tumours of the Littr&eacute; glands of the distal urethra causing mucous secretion may be detected early {13160939; 1113396; 26410973}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:08:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 507,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 546,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69732,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 227,
        "headingId": 546,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Extremely rare tumours have been documented in the literature, with a broad patient age range (30&ndash;66&nbsp;years) {13160939; 1113396; 26410973}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:08:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 508,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 547,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69733,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 227,
        "headingId": 547,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:08:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 509,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 548,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69734,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 227,
        "headingId": 548,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:08:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 516,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 555,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69735,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 227,
        "headingId": 555,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Various macroscopic appearances have been described, ranging from flattened urethral mucosa to friable haemorrhagic tumorous masses in the urethra to deep ulceration on the surface of the shaft of the penis with firm induration of the surrounding soft tissues {13160939; 1113396; 26410973}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:08:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 510,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 549,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69736,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 227,
        "headingId": 549,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Adenocarcinoma with papillary or tubulopapillary architecture. Cells are columnar with voluminous cytoplasm and mucinous vacuoles. Nuclei are large and oval without marked pleomorphism. Information about the immunohistochemical profile is very limited. Neoplastic cells are positive for CK7 and negative for PSA {13160939; 1113396; 26410973}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:08:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 511,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 550,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69737,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 227,
        "headingId": 550,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Urethral secretions have shown cells with fine chromatin and dense cytoplasm with secretory granules containing mucin {26410973}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:08:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 512,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 551,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69738,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 227,
        "headingId": 551,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:08:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 515,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 554,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69739,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 227,
        "headingId": 554,
        "headingText": "<p><em>Essential:</em> the diagnosis of Littr&eacute; gland adenocarcinoma is one of exclusion, so clinical and radiological correlation is required; urothelial carcinoma with extensive glandular differentiation, adenocarcinoma of the bladder and prostate, adenocarcinoma with urethral extension, or colonic metastatic adenocarcinoma should be considered within the differential diagnosis; absence of neoplastic changes in urethral epithelial layer.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> dysplasia or in&nbsp;situ changes within the remaining Littr&eacute; gland.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2022-03-23T12:50:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 513,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 552,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69740,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 227,
        "headingId": 552,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The eighth edition of the American Joint Committee on Cancer (AJCC) and Union for International Cancer Control (UICC) TNM system can be applied.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:08:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 514,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 553,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69741,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 227,
        "headingId": 553,
        "headingText": "<p>Very limited information about the prognosis and biological behaviour of Littr&eacute; gland adenocarcinoma exists in the literature. Prognosis is related to stage. No recurrences or distant metastases after complete resection have been documented {13160939; 1113396; 26410973}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2022-03-23T12:50:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]